<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7666" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">chălāzĭus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χάλαζα</span>, hail, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>pertaining to
			hail</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lapis,</span>”
				<i>a precious stone</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					36, 22, 43, § 157</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">chălā-zĭon</span></b> ,
			ii, n., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χαλάζιον</span>, <i>a pimple</i> or <i>small tubercle on the eyelids</i>, <i><span class="en">Cels. 7, 7,
				2</span></i>, Caption: de chalazio palpebrarum (written as Greek in
			the text).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
